# ============================================================================
# What ships, and what does not
#
# SHIPS
#   code, docs, tests, config, and results/ (the corpora are the only evidence
#   chain this project has — it is not under version control elsewhere, so the
#   harness_snapshot/ trees inside them must not be lost).
#   Data: the ZONE A files the harness actually reads, plus ZONE B truth:
#     data/eval/dataset.json                                  the per-file seal
#     data/eval/<split>/<sc-id>/scenario_id.txt
#     data/eval/<split>/<sc-id>/benchmarks/*.csv
#     data/eval/<split>/<sc-id>/artifacts/**                  ~31 MB, the real input
#     data/truth/**                                           ~236 KB, so others can score
#
# DOES NOT SHIP
#   The bulk claim-count inputs and generator output. Neither is read by the
#   prompt body or by stats_pack.py — both are regenerated by
#   scripts/generate_scenarios.py --scale full.
#
#   KNOWN COST, accepted deliberately: build_prompt() lists every file in a
#   scenario directory, so a clone that lacks these two classes builds prompts
#   that differ byte-wise from the published corpora (the preflight integrity
#   gate still passes: it only re-hashes files that exist). For prompt-level
#   reproduction, regenerate or restore the full tree first.
# ============================================================================

data/raw/
data/eval/**/exposure.csv
data/eval/**/*_claims.csv

# Leakage discipline: ZONE B (data/truth/) is versioned here on purpose so the
# benchmark is scorable by third parties. The invariant that still holds, and is
# enforced at runtime by leakcheck.py + run_zero_shot.preflight_guards(), is that
# nothing from data/truth/ ever reaches a model-facing prompt or data/eval/.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local scratch and stale archives
*.log
.tmp-*
results/*.pid
results/results.7z
